# Lab 11-3 acceptance tests: F_InRange, F_Deadband and FB_SampleStats
# on a two-head check-weigher.
# Tested: one sample per rising edge of HeadNReady (a held signal counts
# once), inclusive limits, empty range when Low > High, limits changed at
# run time, min/max seeded by the first sample after a clear, the mean,
# both instances updating ONE shared LineStats record (also in the same
# scan), per-instance Reject outputs and sample counters, clearing, and
# report-by-exception of the mean with a deadband (including a change of
# exactly the deadband), a record that stays at zero while ClearPB is held,
# and a 0 g sample (empty container) as the minimum.
# Only interface names are used: program I/O and variables, the LineStats
# fields, and Head1/Head2 .Reject .Samples.
# A "sample" is: set the weight, raise HeadNReady for one scan, drop it.

scenario statistics are empty at power-up and nothing is counted by itself
scan
expect LineStats.Count 0
expect LineStats.InSpec 0
expect LineStats.OutSpec 0
expect LineStats.MinValue ~ 0.0 0.001
expect LineStats.MaxValue ~ 0.0 0.001
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 0.0 0.001
expect ReportedMean ~ 0.0 0.001
expect Head1Reject FALSE
expect Head2Reject FALSE
wait 2s
expect LineStats.Count 0
expect Head1.Samples 0
expect Head2.Samples 0

scenario one good weight from head 1
set Head1Weight 500.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect LineStats.Count 1
expect LineStats.InSpec 1
expect LineStats.OutSpec 0
expect LineStats.MinValue ~ 500.0 0.001
expect LineStats.MaxValue ~ 500.0 0.001
expect LineStats.Sum ~ 500.0 0.001
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 500.0 0.001
expect Head1Reject FALSE
expect Head1.Samples 1
expect Head2.Samples 0
wait 1s
expect LineStats.Count 1            # nothing more until the next Ready

scenario a Ready signal held on for many scans is counted once
set Head1Weight 500.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
wait 1s
expect LineStats.Count 1
expect Head1.Samples 1
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
set Head1Weight 502.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
expect LineStats.Count 2
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 501.0 0.001

scenario an out-of-limits weight is rejected by its own head only
set Head2Weight 490.0               # underweight
set Head2Ready TRUE
scan
set Head2Ready FALSE
scan 2
expect Head2Reject TRUE
expect Head1Reject FALSE
expect LineStats.OutSpec 1
expect LineStats.InSpec 0
expect LineStats.Count 1
set Head1Weight 510.0               # overweight on head 1
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan 2
expect Head1Reject TRUE
expect LineStats.OutSpec 2
set Head1Weight 500.0               # a new value arrives, but Ready has not come yet:
scan 3
expect Head1Reject TRUE             # nothing is judged until the Ready edge
expect LineStats.Count 2
set Head2Weight 500.0               # head 2's next container is good
set Head2Ready TRUE
scan
set Head2Ready FALSE
scan 2
expect Head2Reject FALSE
expect Head1Reject TRUE             # head 1 keeps its own result until its next sample
expect LineStats.InSpec 1
expect LineStats.Count 3

scenario the limits are inclusive
set Head1Weight 495.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect Head1Reject FALSE
set Head1Weight 505.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect Head1Reject FALSE
set Head1Weight 494.9
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect Head1Reject TRUE
set Head1Weight 505.1
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect Head1Reject TRUE
expect LineStats.Count 4
expect LineStats.InSpec 2
expect LineStats.OutSpec 2
expect LineStats.MinValue ~ 494.9 0.001
expect LineStats.MaxValue ~ 505.1 0.001

scenario both heads add to the same shared record
set Head1Weight 500.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
set Head2Weight 504.0
set Head2Ready TRUE
scan
set Head2Ready FALSE
scan
set Head1Weight 496.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect LineStats.Count 3
expect LineStats.InSpec 3
expect LineStats.OutSpec 0
expect LineStats.MinValue ~ 496.0 0.001
expect LineStats.MaxValue ~ 504.0 0.001
expect LineStats.Sum ~ 1500.0 0.001
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 500.0 0.001
expect Head1.Samples 2               # each instance keeps its own count...
expect Head2.Samples 1               # ...while both update LineStats

scenario samples from both heads in the same scan are both counted
set Head1Weight 498.0
set Head2Weight 502.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
set Head2Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
set Head2Ready FALSE
scan
expect LineStats.Count 2
expect LineStats.MinValue ~ 498.0 0.001
expect LineStats.MaxValue ~ 502.0 0.001
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 500.0 0.001
expect Head1.Samples 1
expect Head2.Samples 1

scenario clearing empties the shared record but not the per-head counters
set Head1Weight 500.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
set Head2Weight 490.0
set Head2Ready TRUE
scan
set Head2Ready FALSE
scan
set Head1Weight 501.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect LineStats.Count 3
set ClearPB TRUE
scan
set ClearPB FALSE
scan
expect LineStats.Count 0
expect LineStats.InSpec 0
expect LineStats.OutSpec 0
expect LineStats.MinValue ~ 0.0 0.001
expect LineStats.MaxValue ~ 0.0 0.001
expect LineStats.Sum ~ 0.0 0.001
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 0.0 0.001
expect Head1.Samples 2
expect Head2.Samples 1
set Head2Weight 503.0               # first sample after the clear seeds min and max
set Head2Ready TRUE
scan
set Head2Ready FALSE
scan
expect LineStats.Count 1
expect LineStats.MinValue ~ 503.0 0.001
expect LineStats.MaxValue ~ 503.0 0.001
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 503.0 0.001
expect Head2.Samples 2

scenario while ClearPB is held the record stays at zero, even if a weight arrives
set Head1Weight 500.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect LineStats.Count 1
set ClearPB TRUE                    # clear pressed and held...
scan 2
expect LineStats.Count 0
set Head2Weight 490.0               # ...a container is weighed during the clear
set Head2Ready TRUE
scan
expect LineStats.Count 0            # zero on every scan while the button is held
set Head2Ready FALSE
scan 3
expect LineStats.Count 0            # the weight is not added to the cleared record
expect LineStats.OutSpec 0
expect LineStats.MinValue ~ 0.0 0.001
expect LineStats.Sum ~ 0.0 0.001
expect Head2Reject TRUE             # but its reject gate still works
expect Head2.Samples 1
set ClearPB FALSE
scan 2
expect LineStats.Count 0            # releasing the button adds nothing
set Head1Weight 502.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect LineStats.Count 1            # counting starts again after the release
expect LineStats.MinValue ~ 502.0 0.001
expect LineStats.MaxValue ~ 502.0 0.001

scenario an empty container (0 g) is a real sample and becomes the minimum
set Head1Weight 500.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
set Head1Weight 0.0                 # nothing was filled
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect Head1Reject TRUE
set Head1Weight 502.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect LineStats.Count 3
expect LineStats.OutSpec 1
expect LineStats.MinValue ~ 0.0 0.001
expect LineStats.MaxValue ~ 502.0 0.001
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 334.0 0.001

scenario new limits entered on the HMI apply to the next sample
set HighLimit 510.0
set Head1Weight 508.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect Head1Reject FALSE
expect LineStats.InSpec 1
set HighLimit 505.0
set Head1Weight 508.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect Head1Reject TRUE
expect LineStats.OutSpec 1

scenario limits entered the wrong way round make every sample out of limits
set LowLimit 505.0
set HighLimit 495.0
set Head1Weight 500.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan
expect Head1Reject TRUE
expect LineStats.OutSpec 1
expect LineStats.InSpec 0

scenario the reported mean only moves when the mean changes by the deadband or more
set Head1Weight 500.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan 2
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 500.0 0.001
expect ReportedMean ~ 500.0 0.001        # first report
set Head2Weight 500.6
set Head2Ready TRUE
scan
set Head2Ready FALSE
scan 2
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 500.3 0.001
expect ReportedMean ~ 500.0 0.001        # moved 0.3 g: not reported
set Head1Weight 500.6
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan 2
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 500.4 0.001
expect ReportedMean ~ 500.0 0.001        # 0.4 g from the last REPORTED value: not reported
set Head2Weight 502.0
set Head2Ready TRUE
scan
set Head2Ready FALSE
scan 2
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 500.8 0.001
expect ReportedMean ~ 500.8 0.001        # 0.8 g: reported
set Head1Weight 496.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan 2
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 499.84 0.001
expect ReportedMean ~ 499.84 0.001       # 0.96 g downwards: reported
set Head2Weight 500.2
set Head2Ready TRUE
scan
set Head2Ready FALSE
scan 2
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 499.9 0.001
expect ReportedMean ~ 499.84 0.001       # 0.06 g: not reported
wait 2s
expect ReportedMean ~ 499.84 0.001       # and it does not creep between samples
set MeanDeadband 0.0                     # a zero band passes every change
scan 2
expect ReportedMean ~ 499.9 0.001

scenario a change of exactly the deadband is reported
set Head1Weight 500.0
set Head1Ready TRUE
scan
set Head1Ready FALSE
scan 2
expect ReportedMean ~ 500.0 0.001
set Head2Weight 501.0
set Head2Ready TRUE
scan
set Head2Ready FALSE
scan 2
expect LineStats.Mean ~ 500.5 0.001
expect ReportedMean ~ 500.5 0.001        # moved by exactly 0.5 g: "by Band or more"
